    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. The declaration arm (cpp.py:2838-2870) never checks the declarator's shape, so every local whose type names a class is read as a stack construction. `T* p;`, `T& r = s;` and `T* q = get();` each emit instantiates -> T with evidence stack_construction; `T* p = new T(1);` emits it beside the new edge. Nothing is constructed. r20, v04."  # 16d2
